course: dictionary
lesson: 11056
title: The word week
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A week is seven days. You can find its meaning from the words around it. In «He looks after the new fish every week», the word every tells you he does it again and again, once each seven days.
explain: In «Saving means putting money aside, week after week, until you have enough», the words week after week tell you the saving goes on and on, one week after another. Swap in seven days: "putting money aside, seven days after seven days" is a little clumsy, but the meaning is clear.
explain: In «A girl in Ireland gave up the piano after one hard week», the word week is one stretch of seven days, and the word hard tells you those days were difficult. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A week is seven days, from Monday to Sunday or from Sunday to Saturday.
fact: The school week means the school or work days, Monday to Friday.
fact: «Weekend» means Saturday and Sunday.
fact: «Weeks» can also mean a long time that you do not count, as in «I haven't seen him for weeks».
fact: A fortnight means two weeks, and «fortnightly» means every two weeks.
exercise: «He looks after the new fish every week.» How often does he look after the fish? | Never | Only once, on a Sunday | Just for one afternoon | *Once every seven days, again and again
exercise: How many days are in one week? | *Seven | Twelve | Ten | Five
exercise: «I haven't seen him for weeks.» What does weeks mean here? | Exactly two days | A cold day | *A long time, not counted | Monday to Friday only
test: «A fortnight» means how many weeks? | *Two | Four | One | Three
test: Which days make up the school week? | *Monday to Friday | Saturday and Sunday | Sunday to Saturday | Every day of the year
exam: Which word means every two weeks? | *Fortnightly | Weekly | Per week | Per annum
